From: ios-sweet Windows/QEMU port
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: QEMU network (virtio-net, boot-arg sweetvnet=1) + clock from the PL031 (sweetrtc=1)

QEMU has no network the phone port can use, and no IORTC: the calendar
started at 1970, which also makes every TLS certificate "not yet valid".

sweet_vnet.c drives a QEMU virt virtio-mmio network device (virtio 1.x,
polled from a kernel thread every 2 ms, 64 x 2 KiB RX/TX buffers, no
offloads) as the kernel ethernet interface en1, with the same ifnet glue
as the phone's USB ECM ue0. It sets 10.0.2.15/24 and a default route to
10.0.2.2 for QEMU's user-mode network (QEMU's DNS proxy is 10.0.2.3).
Started from sweet_ufs_init in ufsvirtio mode.

With sweetrtc=1, IOKitInitializeTime sets the calendar from the QEMU virt
PL031 RTC (0x09010000, data register = host UTC seconds).

Without the boot-args nothing changes.

